cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it
  using the metadata in this file, and cite the TSE electoral
  data you analysed as a separate data source.
type: software
title: "BRElections.jl: a Julia interface to Brazilian electoral open data (TSE)"
abstract: >-
  Julia package for Brazil's public electoral data, published by the Tribunal
  Superior Eleitoral (TSE): candidates, votes, assets, campaign finance,
  voter profiles and polling places (with coordinates) from the open-data
  repository, several years and states per call, each table carrying its
  provenance and ready ABNT, APA or BibTeX references for the data;
  live vote counting from the TSE's results system; and a crosswalk between
  TSE and IBGE municipality codes. It handles downloads with retries, a
  portable local cache revalidated against the TSE, streaming ZIP extraction
  with ISO-8859-1 to UTF-8 transcoding in constant memory, multithreaded CSV
  reading with column selection and row filtering during import, and type
  conversion tuned to TSE conventions (dates, #NULO#/#NE# sentinels, money
  columns with either decimal separator, and identifier columns kept as
  String so leading zeros survive).
authors:
